1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,500
AI can produce more. But can your team respond better?

2
00:00:05,500 --> 00:00:10,000
A stockpile of generated code is still a stockpile.

3
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:16,000
Just-in-Time is the other pillar of the Toyota Production System.

4
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:22,000
Only what is needed, when needed, in the amount needed.

5
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:27,000
Minimum stock. Dependable flow. Not constant activity.

6
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:33,000
JIT entrusts capable people to respond to real need.

7
00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:38,000
Be resourceful with what you have.

8
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:42,500
Pull a small customer problem, not a queue of technical tasks.

9
00:00:42,500 --> 00:00:47,000
Let one useful, end-to-end outcome pull the necessary work.

10
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:50,000
Use AI for what this need requires.

11
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:56,000
Check known quality in the shared, working product.

12
00:00:56,000 --> 00:01:02,000
Use feedback to choose again. Leave later work unstarted.

13
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:08,000
Integrate small changes continuously. Keep one coherent product.

14
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:13,000
When a dependency becomes real, let it pull collaboration.

15
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:18,000
Technical excellence makes that response dependable.

16
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:23,000
Build capability to respond, not stockpiles of generated answers.
